WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.334
-Now the Republicans have

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.934
a slim majority in the House,

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:06.067
they've made it clear
they will use that power

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:08.434
to protect Donald Trump
and go after Joe Biden.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:11.467
And, to do that, they've put
several far-right extremists

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.734
who tried to overthrow
the 2020 election,

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:15.400
including
Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.801
on key committees with the power
to investigate the White House.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:19.767
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:23.901
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:27.167
Republicans still cannot seem
to grasp the differences

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:28.367
between the small number

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:29.901
of classified documents
that were discovered

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.334
at President Biden's home
and office

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:33.000
and the much larger pile
of documents

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.501
Trump stashed at Mar-A-Lago
and refused to give back.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.501
In fact, they keep asking
the same dumb question --

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:40.467
why won't the FBI search
Biden's home,

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.734
just like they searched
Trump's beach resort?

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:46.033
-What's real concerning to me
is how justice is applied

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:47.567
and is it applied equally?

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:49.567
Why do you raid President Trump?

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.100
-[ Southern accent ]
My concern is how

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.033
[ Laughter ]
there's such a discrepancy

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:54.934
in how former President Trump
was treated --

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.834
by raiding Mar-A-Lago,
by getting the security cameras,

00:00:57.834 --> 00:01:00.801
by taking pictures of documents
on the floor,

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:02.834
by going
through Melania's closet.

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:04.734
-Alright, first of all,
Melania's Closet sounds like

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.834
a store you'd find at a mall
in the '90s.

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:08.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.934
Wear the only clothes that
give you that Melania smile.

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:13.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.968
They could've also called it
Cold Topic.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:23.434
Also, I doubt Melania
only has one closet.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.667
My guess is she has multiple
closets for clothes

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.534
and also a secret closet
that lets her escape

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:29.701
out the back, like...

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.400
[ Laughter ]
whenever Trump tries
to talk to her.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.734
[ As Trump ]
Mel!

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:34.234
[ Laughter ]
Mel, I'd love to get

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:35.801
your thoughts
on this speech, Mel.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:36.534
Mel?

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:37.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:40.067
Mel, did you flee
to Narnia again?

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:41.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.801
Give my best to Aslan.

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:43.901
Aslan the Lion.

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:45.567
We love Aslan the lion,
don't we?

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.133
[ Laughter and applause ]
We love him, don't we?

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.934
He came up to me once, folks,
big lion, strong lion...

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:54.033
...tears running down his face
and onto his whiskers,

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:55.567
and he said --
I'll never forget it.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.067
He said to me, "Mr. Trump..."

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:59.167
-[ Roaring ]

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:02.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.868
[ Cheering ]

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.634
Also, I don't have
any trouble believing

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:08.834
that Trump would hide classified
documents in a closet,

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:11.434
the way a teenager hides porns
in a shoebox.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:13.501
[ As Trump ]
They'll never find this,
especially if it's labeled...

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:18.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.200
[ Gruff voice ]
That's how we hid porn
in the old days.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.133
Back when we had
physical pornography.

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:26.200
Now, it's all digital, but you
lose that tactile experience.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.501
[ Laughter ]
That's why people

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:29.567
are getting back
into analog media, these days.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:30.868
You know how everyone's
collecting vinyl

00:02:30.868 --> 00:02:32.067
and cassette tapes again?

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:34.033
Well, I just stayed
at a very classy Airbnb

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:35.901
in upstate New York
that had a beautiful

00:02:35.901 --> 00:02:38.701
mid-century credenza filled
with vintage Hustlers.

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:40.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:41.667
And I'll tell you,
there's nothing better,

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:43.200
after a long day
of apple picking,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.667
than settling
into an Eames chair

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.300
with some good
old-fashioned pornography.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.734
[ Laughter ]
And the articles!

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:51.400
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.467
Again, I cannot
underscore enough

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:54.534
how different these cases are.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:55.901
Biden is discovered

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:57.801
and turned over
about 20 documents, so far.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:03:00.467
And let's be clear --
documents he should not have!

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:01.834
While Trump had over 300.

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:02.934
Trump refused,
for more than a year,

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:03.934
to turn them all over,

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.334
lied about having
turned them over,

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:06.934
instructed staffers to lie,

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.634
moved them around,
claimed they were his,

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:11.534
and claimed he could declassify
them with his mind.

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:13.234
[ Laughter ]
He did the classic Trump thing

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:16.000
of trying every defense,
instead of just one.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.033
[ Laughter ]
Just today, Trump claimed,
on his social media site,

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:19.934
that "Trump hating
Marxist thugs"

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:21.701
had planted
classified documents,

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.067
while also admitting he kept...

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:30.934
[ Laughter ]
Wait. I'm sorry, your story is

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:34.234
you kept an empty folder
as a cool keepsake?

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:36.601
Were they Lisa Frank folders?

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:38.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:41.167
Who keeps an empty folder
as a keepsake?!

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:43.868
When I left "SNL,"
I took plenty of keepsakes,

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:46.234
but one of them wasn't a stack
of loose-leaf paper

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:47.501
from the copier.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.767
Hey, you guys remember
the famous cowbell sketch?

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:51.934
It was printed on paper,
just like this.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:55.167
Also, you don't get
to just take stuff

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:56.968
from the White House
as a cool keepsake.

00:03:56.968 --> 00:04:00.367
It's a government institution
owned by the American people.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:01.601
When you visited Philadelphia,

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:04.033
did you also try to take home
the Liberty Bell?

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:06.200
[ As Trump ]
Just strap it to the roof
of Air Force One.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:09.634
But the differences
don't matter to Republicans.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.400
They've made it clear
they want to weaponize

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.000
congressional committees
to go after Biden.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.934
In fact, the guy you just saw
in that last clip,

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.167
James Comer,
is the new GOP chair

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:19.467
of the House
Oversight Committee.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:22.334
Last year, he told CNN
investigating Trump's

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:24.901
classified documents
was not a priority,

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:27.868
but now, investigating Biden's
very much is a priority.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:30.501
So, CNN's Jake Tapper
asked Comer him to explain

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:31.934
the contradiction,
and he couldn't.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:35.167
-What do you say to viewers
who don't understand

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:36.968
why President Biden's documents

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:39.267
seem like
a big priority for you,

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:42.701
but President Trump, who took
hundreds more documents,

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:44.601
did not comply
with the subpoena,

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:46.767
did not reach out
to the National Archives

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:48.167
or the Justice Department,
to say,

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:50.868
"Hey, we found these documents,"
it's not a priority?

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:51.968
Do you only care

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:53.901
about classified documents
being mishandled

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:55.667
when Democrats
do the mishandling?

00:04:58.133 --> 00:04:59.567
[ Laughter ]
-Absolutely not.

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.434
Look, we still don't know

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.834
what type of documents
President Trump had.

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:06.601
-Yeah, we don't know exactly,
but we know they exist, right?

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:07.901
They released a picture.

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:09.067
You remember that.

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:10.501
This one, that looks like
it's from the

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:12.934
classified document buffet
at Mar-A-Lago.

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:15.167
[ Laughter ]
"I will have an omelet
with ham and cheese

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:17.734
and some of the
nuclear documents."

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:20.801
[ Laughter ]
Also, we don't know
every document Trump has,

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:22.834
but we don't know
what Biden has, either.

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:24.167
And, honestly, I'm shocked

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:25.834
Biden didn't just
throw them all out

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:28.734
because he definitely strikes me
as one of those old dads

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.133
who gets fed up
with all the [bleep]

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:31.734
[ Laughter ]
everyone else left in the garage

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:33.434
and throws it all in a Dumpster.

00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:35.367
"Hey, Dad,
where's my old Schwinn?"

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:38.300
[ As Biden ]
Chopped it up with a saw,
threw it in the garbage.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.534
[ Laughter ]
Needed room for my new Harley.

00:05:39.534 --> 00:05:40.601
You should see your mother and I

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.000
pull up at Applebee's
on that thing.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.701
[ Laughter ]
They give us free potstickers.

00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:45.033
[ Applause ]

00:05:45.033 --> 00:05:47.234
Trump, on the other hand,
strikes me as a hoarder.

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:50.100
I bet he still has every piece
of sports memorabilia

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:53.334
he's ever collected in his life,
no matter how worthless it is.

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:54.567
[ As Trump ]
This right here is very special.

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:56.634
It's a football signed
by Vinny Testaverde.

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:58.701
Not the Vinny Testaverde,

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:01.767
just a guy from Long Island
with the same name.

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:05.000
Did the grouting
on my bathroom tiles.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.000
Great guy.
Still haven't paid him.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.267
[ Laughter and applause ]
So, that's the new chair

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:12.434
of the powerful
House Oversight Committee,

00:06:12.434 --> 00:06:14.501
which has the ability
to issue subpoenas

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.567
and investigate
the administration.

00:06:16.567 --> 00:06:18.400
In fact, Comer just sent
a request

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:19.701
to the Biden administration

00:06:19.701 --> 00:06:22.400
requesting visitor logs
for Biden's Delaware home,

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.334
which was an odd request,
given that people don't usually

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:27.667
keep visitor logs
for private residences.

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:30.234
I mean, I do,
but that's only so I

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:32.634
can remember all the celebrities
that stopped by

00:06:32.634 --> 00:06:34.467
for my famous dinner parties.

00:06:34.467 --> 00:06:36.434
Let's take a look
at the first page.

00:06:36.434 --> 00:06:39.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:44.667
Anyway, it turns out that Biden

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:47.801
does not keep visitor logs
for his private residence.

00:06:47.801 --> 00:06:49.300
-Some news this morning.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:54.167
We are learning there are
no visitor logs chronicling

00:06:54.167 --> 00:06:57.734
who comes and goes from the
president's house in Wilmington.

00:06:57.734 --> 00:06:58.968
-Yeah, of course there aren't.

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:01.734
It's a house,
not a bed &amp; breakfast.

00:07:01.734 --> 00:07:04.567
[ Laughter ]
Although, I would like to see
Biden open up B&amp;B.

00:07:04.567 --> 00:07:06.067
[ As Biden ]
Alright, here are the rules.

00:07:06.067 --> 00:07:08.133
Breakfast starts at 4:00
and ends at 4:30.

00:07:08.133 --> 00:07:09.467
[ Laughter ]
The closest we got
to oat milk is

00:07:09.467 --> 00:07:11.501
what's left over
after I eat my Cheerios,

00:07:11.501 --> 00:07:14.167
so, unless you want that
in your coffee, shut your yap!

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.567
[ Laughter ]
At 6:00, we go out back
to chop wood

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:18.567
and then we spend the rest
of the day watching "Matlock."

00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:19.501
Oh, and if you're interested,

00:07:19.501 --> 00:07:20.801
there's Hustlers
in the credenza.

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:23.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.767
Also, real talk.

00:07:25.767 --> 00:07:28.467
You want to know why there are
no visitor logs in Wilmington?

00:07:28.467 --> 00:07:30.834
No one wants to admit

00:07:30.834 --> 00:07:32.234
they were ever in Wilmington.

00:07:32.234 --> 00:07:34.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:34.367 --> 00:07:36.100
Hey, it's all jokes, Delaware.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.968
You know I love you.
I love your beaches,

00:07:37.968 --> 00:07:40.000
your corporate tax shelters,
and the Amtrak station

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.601
I pass through on my way
from New York to D.C.

00:07:42.601 --> 00:07:44.501
It's like the commercials say --
Delaware.

00:07:44.501 --> 00:07:45.634
It's better than Jersey.

00:07:45.634 --> 00:07:46.501
Barely.

00:07:46.501 --> 00:07:49.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:49.133 --> 00:07:51.901
So, those are the kinds of dumb
requests the Oversight Committee

00:07:51.901 --> 00:07:53.100
will, apparently,
be obsessed with,

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.300
now that Republicans are
in charge.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:57.367
The bummer is some actual
oversight would be great.

00:07:57.367 --> 00:08:00.067
Congress should hold
the administration accountable,

00:08:00.067 --> 00:08:01.200
regardless of party.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.133
They should just do it
for real stuff

00:08:03.133 --> 00:08:04.200
that people actually care about.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.634
Instead, House Speaker
Kevin McCarthy

00:08:05.634 --> 00:08:08.067
has appointed some of his
caucus' looniest weirdos

00:08:08.067 --> 00:08:09.400
to both
the Oversight Committee,

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.000
where they will have the power
to investigate Biden;

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.367
and also the powerful
Homeland Security Committee.

00:08:13.367 --> 00:08:15.133
-McCarthy made big promises

00:08:15.133 --> 00:08:16.734
to Congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:08:16.734 --> 00:08:18.634
and Paul Gosar,
two hardliners, of course,

00:08:18.634 --> 00:08:20.267
who were kicked off
of their committees

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:22.868
by Democrats last session.

00:08:22.868 --> 00:08:25.634
They are back on some pretty
prominent committees, in fact.

00:08:25.634 --> 00:08:27.100
Oversight,
the House Oversight Committee,

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.467
very, very powerful,
will now include

00:08:29.467 --> 00:08:31.501
Marjorie Taylor Greene,
Lauren Boebert,

00:08:31.501 --> 00:08:33.701
Scott Perry, and Paul Gosar.

00:08:33.701 --> 00:08:36.100
So, again, some big
hardliner names

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:38.667
that are going to be serving
in a very powerful position.

00:08:38.667 --> 00:08:40.801
-There is Congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:08:40.801 --> 00:08:41.968
There's Paul Gosar.

00:08:41.968 --> 00:08:44.100
Those two were thrown
off their committees

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:46.434
in the last two years by the
Democratic-controlled Congress

00:08:46.434 --> 00:08:49.000
for incendiary
an/or violent rhetoric.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.801
They will get committee
assignments back.

00:08:50.801 --> 00:08:53.234
In fact, we can confirm
that Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:08:53.234 --> 00:08:55.267
will be on the Committee
on Homeland Security.

00:08:55.267 --> 00:08:57.200
That's a coveted spot.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.734
-That's right,
a bunch of people who tried

00:08:58.734 --> 00:09:00.434
to overthrow the 2020 election

00:09:00.434 --> 00:09:01.968
will now sit on major committees

00:09:01.968 --> 00:09:04.434
with the power to investigate
the administration,

00:09:04.434 --> 00:09:06.267
which, to me, does not seem
like a great idea.

00:09:06.267 --> 00:09:08.767
It's like if you're a prosecutor
in a murder trial,

00:09:08.767 --> 00:09:10.200
you wouldn't want
to show up to court

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.767
and see a guy in a hockey mask
sitting in the jury box.

00:09:12.767 --> 00:09:14.701
[ Laughter ]
"Ah, son of a gun.

00:09:14.701 --> 00:09:15.801
How did we miss him?"

00:09:15.801 --> 00:09:16.767
[ Laughter and awws ]

00:09:16.767 --> 00:09:17.801
It's especially insane

00:09:17.801 --> 00:09:18.968
to put Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:09:18.968 --> 00:09:20.067
on the Homeland Security
Committee,

00:09:20.067 --> 00:09:21.567
given that she has
previously espoused

00:09:21.567 --> 00:09:23.501
some pretty unhinged
conspiracy theories,

00:09:23.501 --> 00:09:24.901
like the time she, of course,

00:09:24.901 --> 00:09:28.234
claimed the 2018 California
wildfires were caused by...

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.167
[ Laughter ]
She shouldn't be on the
Homeland Security Committee.

00:09:45.167 --> 00:09:47.100
She should be an actor
with one line

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.467
in the next "Avengers" movie.

00:09:48.467 --> 00:09:49.834
[ Laughter ]

00:09:49.834 --> 00:09:51.734
[ As Greene ]
Thanos is collecting
the sun's energy

00:09:51.734 --> 00:09:54.501
and beaming it to the Earth
to cause wildfires.

00:09:54.501 --> 00:09:56.667
Also, we think Thanos
might be Jewish.

00:09:56.667 --> 00:09:57.534
"Cut!

00:09:57.534 --> 00:10:00.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:00.567 --> 00:10:02.534
That second part isn't
in the script."

00:10:02.534 --> 00:10:04.767
I know, but doesn't it make it

00:10:04.767 --> 00:10:06.801
[ Laughter ]
sound more believable?

00:10:06.801 --> 00:10:08.834
Greene also spread
conspiracy theories

00:10:08.834 --> 00:10:11.734
about everything
from the COVID vaccine to 9/11

00:10:11.734 --> 00:10:13.534
and, when she was asked
about her past support

00:10:13.534 --> 00:10:15.267
for QAnon,
she blamed the Internet.

00:10:15.267 --> 00:10:17.400
-The Democrats stripped you
of your committee assignments

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:18.334
after you were elected.
-Right.

00:10:18.334 --> 00:10:19.868
-That was raw politics.
-Mm-hmm.

00:10:19.868 --> 00:10:22.434
-But, in fairness, didn't you
also say, around that period,

00:10:22.434 --> 00:10:24.734
that you had been a follower
of QAnon conspiracy theories

00:10:24.734 --> 00:10:25.901
and you had rethought this

00:10:25.901 --> 00:10:28.400
and you were no longer
influenced by the group?

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.267
-Well, like a lot
of people today,

00:10:30.267 --> 00:10:32.667
I had easily gotten sucked
into some things

00:10:32.667 --> 00:10:34.000
I'd seen on the Internet.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.400
-I'm not sure I'm comfortable
having someone

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.267
on one of Congress'
most sensitive committees

00:10:37.267 --> 00:10:39.200
who gets sucked into things
they see on the Internet.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.767
That's the same excuse
your mom uses

00:10:40.767 --> 00:10:42.834
when she spends 1,000 bucks
on Candy Crush.

00:10:42.834 --> 00:10:44.234
[ Laughter ]
Mom, again?!

00:10:44.234 --> 00:10:46.501
"I got sucked into buying
more lollipop hammers,

00:10:46.501 --> 00:10:48.434
so I could finally be
the Jelly Queen.

00:10:48.434 --> 00:10:51.734
[ Laughter ]
Now, Venmo your mother
some money."

00:10:51.734 --> 00:10:53.234
[ Laughter ]

00:10:53.234 --> 00:10:54.834
But this was part
of the deal McCarthy made

00:10:54.834 --> 00:10:56.868
with the crazies in his caucus
to become speaker.

00:10:56.868 --> 00:10:58.334
Remember,
Greene threw her support

00:10:58.334 --> 00:11:01.100
behind McCarthy specifically
because she wanted to get

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:03.234
on these powerful committees,
which she bragged about

00:11:03.234 --> 00:11:05.334
in MAGA rallies
before the election.

00:11:05.334 --> 00:11:06.934
-I'm looking forward
to Republicans

00:11:06.934 --> 00:11:08.934
taking back control
in the House.

00:11:08.934 --> 00:11:09.734
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:11:09.734 --> 00:11:10.834
And I'm looking forward

00:11:10.834 --> 00:11:12.501
to serving on committees.

00:11:12.501 --> 00:11:14.701
-It is unnerving
when someone says the phrase,

00:11:14.701 --> 00:11:16.267
"I'm looking forward
to serving on committees"

00:11:16.267 --> 00:11:18.267
with that much glee.
It's like hearing someone say,

00:11:18.267 --> 00:11:20.634
"I'm looking forward to visiting
Wilmington, Delaware."

00:11:20.634 --> 00:11:22.133
I'm kidding, Delaware.
I love you guys.

00:11:22.133 --> 00:11:23.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:23.868 --> 00:11:25.701
Philly, on the other hand...

00:11:25.701 --> 00:11:28.167
[ Laughter ]
Donald Trump

00:11:28.167 --> 00:11:30.501
tanked his party
in three successive elections,

00:11:30.501 --> 00:11:32.067
leaving the GOP weak
and fractured,

00:11:32.067 --> 00:11:34.300
but what we're seeing right now
in the House

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:36.300
are the last vestiges
of Trumpism.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.267
McCarthy and the
far-right extremists

00:11:38.267 --> 00:11:40.334
he's empowered in the House
have made it clear

00:11:40.334 --> 00:11:42.534
they're going to use their
positions to protect Trump,

00:11:42.534 --> 00:11:43.968
who stashed classified documents

00:11:43.968 --> 00:11:47.000
the way a teenager would stash
a magazine called...

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.601
-Melania's closet.

00:11:48.601 --> 00:11:50.234
[ Laughter ]

00:11:50.234 --> 00:11:52.267
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:52.267 --> 00:11:53.734
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:11:53.734 --> 00:11:55.968
♪♪
[ Whistling ]

